One more check — is there anywhere else in packages/react (outside of the compose-refs package itself) that creates an inline ref callback that captures render-scope state and is attached to an element? The user specifically asked about "the same pattern" — i.e., a non-memoized composeRefs. I've identified all call sites of composeRefs(. To be thorough about the "pattern," I should also check for inline `ref={(node) => setState(node)}` style callbacks that get recreated every render — but that's a broader class (every inline ref arrow). The bug specifically concerns composed refs that get re-attached on every render. Inline `ref={(node) => ...}` that calls setState is actually a known React anti-pattern in its own right, but it's not "the same pattern" (not a composed ref). I'll limit to the composeRefs pattern (what the user asked: "the same pattern" = the pattern I found in slot: composeRefs creating an unstable identity every render), and I can mention the inline ref arrow in nav-menu as something covered by the fix.

